  "improvements": [
    "Confirmed a 90%-filled USD 5bn maximum operation without settlement date produced TGA cash-out labels even while its cash verification flag was false. Current operation/day labels describe large high fill only.",
    "The additive auction-buyback-fill.v1 contract records the exact par thresholds, consumed values, descriptive role and false qualification flags. The existing liquidity_signal field remains as an explicitly deprecated compatibility alias; it does not measure liquidity.",
    "Explicit cash-effect context retains the reported date but leaves cash settlement, net reserves and duration DV01 unmeasured, listing the missing inputs. No policy impulse, expected return, Calls, sizing or execution authority is inferred.",
    "Offline replay validates all new semantics. A narrow compatibility branch reconstructs old supplied arithmetic and its exact legacy labels without executing predecessor code or qualifying those labels. Partially supplied or altered new metadata fails.",
    "The page maps the two exact unsupported legacy labels to cash effect unmeasured without changing retained packets. Full operation evidence includes new classification and cash metadata, and remains escaped and keyboard accessible.",
    "Legacy downloads now use a Blob of the exact received UTF-8 bytes, including whitespace and key order, and a displayed SHA-256. They do not refetch the mutable public packet. Missing download facilities hide the control rather than substitute another publication.",
    "The link and desk update together. Failed rendering releases only the rejected incoming download; transport failure preserves the previous link; successful refresh revokes the old Blob URL. Late responses cannot discard the displayed source. Compact manifest-bound downloads remain unchanged."
  ],
